{"availability":"available","full":"volkerp/flaskrqdemo","name":"flaskrqdemo","description":"This project ties together Flask, Redis, RQ (Redis Queue), Docker in a simple demo application.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":26,"forks":5,"created":"2019-06-21T16:38:55Z","updated":"2023-02-02T06:31:21Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["docker-compose","docker-containers","flask","python","redis","redis-queue","rq","rq-dashboard"],"demo":"http://flask.pocoo.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T00:01:42.429Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T00:01:42.429Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T00:01:42.429Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T00:01:42.429Z","stars":26,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project ties together Flask, Redis, RQ (Redis Queue) and Docker in a simple demo application. It can serve as template for other projects as well as an introduction on how to use Flask with RQ while managing it all with docker-compose.","In the web application you can launch long running jobs which are put into a RQ task queue. From there a RQ worker picks it up and executes it. During execution the job reports back some progress information and – if execution was successful – the job result."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/volkerp/flaskrqdemo/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"24c323f2bcf9fbf27e42c6ca05634a010a840e99cff7420af611d5a1c03718d4","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T00:01:42.535Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T00:01:42.535Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project ties together Flask, Redis, RQ (Redis Queue) and Docker in a simple demo application. It can serve as template for other projects as well as an introduction on how to use Flask with RQ while managing it all with docker-compose.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/volkerp/flaskrqdemo/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"24c323f2b